Speech: Open Speech Repository (Telchemy), Harvard sentences, free to use, copy and publish. Credit: "Open Speech Repository". Encoded to Codec 2 3200 with src/tdma_console/tools/c2clip.py: OSR_0010_F.c2 (MASTER, OSR_us_000_0010_8k.wav), OSR_0030_M.c2 (SEC 1, OSR_us_000_0030_8k.wav), OSR_0011_F.c2 (SEC 2, OSR_us_000_0011_8k.wav), OSR_0031_M.c2 (SEC 3, OSR_us_000_0031_8k.wav, added 2026-10-30).

Opus clips for 80-byte payload builds (docs/opus_payload.md), from the same recordings with `c2clip.py opus`: SILK narrowband, 7.2 kbit/s CBR, SILK forced, complexity 2, four 18 B frames per 72 B chunk. OSR_0010_F.op72, OSR_0030_M.op72, OSR_0011_F.op72, OSR_0031_M.op72; chunk k is the same 80 ms of speech as chunk k of the .c2 clip. Their lossless decodes (<clip>_op72_ref.wav) regenerate with the same command.
